override formatMessage to use a temporary message? Hmm.\n\nAlternative approach: compute formatted prefix separately. The format is _FORMAT which uses %(message)s. Simplest clean approach: create a shallow copy of record with copy.copy, set copy.msg=truncated, copy.args=(), then call super().format(copy). But super().format would also compute record.message etc on copy; and exc_info/stack_info preserved on copy. Also other custom attributes (keep_full_message) copied. That's clean. Wait: Formatter.format on copy sets copy.message; fine.\n\nBut careful: copying a LogRecord with copy.copy copies __dict__ shallowly — fine.\n\nHowever the multiline handling uses record.message from the copy; in our format method after super().format(record) we use record.message. Let's restructure:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    if <limit applies>:\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        limited = self._limit(message)\n        if limited != message:\n            record = copy.copy(record)\n            record.msg = limited\n            record.args = ()\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    ...\n```\n\nWait but super().format(record) with record.msg full and no args -> message = limited. record.message = limited. Multiline prefix logic uses record.message → good.\n\nCareful: copy.copy retains exc_info yes.\n\nTruncation math: marker = \"...<omitted>...\" len 15. If len(message) <= budget return. remain = budget - 15. head = ceil(remain/2) = (remain+1)//2, tail = remain - head. Return message[:head] + marker + (message[-tail:] if tail else \"\"). If remain <= 0? budget>=32 so remain>=17; fine.\n\nmax_message_chars validation: must be int, not bool, >= 32, or None. else ValueError.\n\n_setup_logger: pass max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS — need import envs from deepinfer.environ in logger.py. Check for circular import: environ.py imports only stdlib. logger.py importing deepinfer.environ at module level... environ imports nothing from logger, so fine. But logger.py imports at top; environ.py might import others? Only stdlib from what we saw. Use local import inside _setup_logger to be safe? Module-level import is fine but local import avoids potential cycles. I'll do module-level `from deepinfer.environ import envs` — hmm, deepinfer package __init__ may import things causing cycle. Safer: inside _setup_logger do `from deepinfer.environ import envs`. Do that.\n\nNow let's check that environ.py already has the entry: need to verify. Let me read environ.py around logging section, and then edit logger.py in the same action? Better: first check environ, then edit. Budget: 4 requests left. Combine: read environ section + apply logger edits in one action? Edits to logger.py don't depend on environ read except knowing the attribute name, which I'll set myself. But if environ is wrong I need to fix.\n\nLet me do: read environ env var section (search via search_code for \"LOG_MAX_MESSAGE\"), and edit logger.py in the same action.\n\nActually order: search first, print; then edits. Fine — single python block with both.\n\nFor stats_logger: logger.info(m) → logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True}).\n\nLet me write the logger edits carefully with replace_text.\n\nOld text 1 (init):\n```\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n```\nNew:\n```\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        if max_message_chars is not None and (\n            isinstance(max_message_chars, bool)\n            or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int)\n            or max_message_chars < _MIN_MESSAGE_BUDGET\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= {_MIN_MESSAGE_BUDGET} or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\"\n            )\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nAdd constants after _COLOR_RESET:\n```\n_MESSAGE_OMITTED = \"...<omitted>...\"\n_MIN_MESSAGE_BUDGET = 32\n```\n\nAdd methods before format:\n\n```\n    def _limit_message(self, message: str) -> str:\n        budget = self.max_message_chars\n        if budget is None or len(message) <= budget:\n            return message\n        remaining = budget - len(_MESSAGE_OMITTED)\n        head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n        tail = remaining - head\n        suffix = message[-tail:] if tail > 0 else \"\"\n        return f\"{message[:head]}{_MESSAGE_OMITTED}{suffix}\"\n```\n\nAnd format.\n\nAlso import copy at top.\n\nThen _setup_logger fmt:\n```\n    from deepinfer.environ import envs\n\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )\n```\n\nNow verify environ has env item. Let's run search_code + edits.\n\nNote replace_text requires old_text unique. Let's do."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 9285, "completion_tokens": 2169, "total_tokens": 11454, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4096}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 2010}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4096, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 5189}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
